# Agent context bootstrap (DB routes, markdown payloads)

The workspace SQLite index (`.md/workspace_index.sqlite`, STRATA) is the **genesis point for discovery**. Markdown handoffs, blueprints, and plans are the **payload** — read in full only after the index narrows candidates.

<HARD-GATE>
Before **Plan** or **Build** on any non-trivial task (more than a one-file trivial edit), run this sequence in order. Skip only for pure Q&A about visible code or when this session already ran the sequence for the same task.
</HARD-GATE>

## Bootstrap sequence

| Step | Action | MCP tool (`workspace-knowledge`) | Fallback |
|------|--------|----------------------------------|----------|
| 1 | Blueprint for the active repo | `knowledge_blueprint(project)` | Read `.md/blueprints/<repo>.md` |
| 2 | Recent handoffs (48h window) | `knowledge_recent(project, kind=handoff, hours=48)` | STRATA app search (`strata app --open`) |
| 3 | Cross-project prior art | `knowledge_graph_neighbors(path_or_query="<one-line task>")` | STRATA app graph view |
| 4 | FTS fallback if step 3 is empty or all weights &lt; 0.15 | `knowledge_search(query)` | STRATA app search |
| 5 | Deep read survivors only | `knowledge_get(path)` or **Read** the file | Read the file on disk (storage=file only) |

Use **free-text** for step 3 (task description), not a doc path — path mode is for when you already know the anchor document.

## Thresholds and discipline

- Treat graph hits with `link_type: explicit` or `weight >= 0.15` as prior art — read before designing.
- Weaker graph hits are noise; do not pad plans with marginal references.
- After steps 3–4, read **full bodies only for the 2–5 best candidates** — not every search hit.
- If prior art solves the problem, **reuse and cite** the doc in plan/handoff instead of re-deriving.
- If prior art shows a failed approach, say what differs this time.
- Valid outcome: note briefly "no prior art found" and proceed.

## Do not

- **Do not** grep or walk `.md/handoff/**`, `.md/blueprints/**`, or `.cursor/plans/**` for discovery — use the index.
- **Do not** use the file tree as the entry point for cross-repo context.

## Archived and storage modes

| `storage` | Read full body via |
|-----------|-------------------|
| `file` (active handoff, &lt; ~96h) | `knowledge_get` or **Read** on disk path |
| `db_only` (archived handoff, pruned plan) | **`knowledge_get` only** — disk path may not exist |

## MCP unavailable

If `workspace-knowledge` MCP is not connected, use the STRATA localhost app (`strata app --open`) for search and graph — do not skip bootstrap and grep instead.

## Index freshness

If queries miss documents you know exist, index before falling back to file-tree search:

```bash
strata index
# or STRATA app → Files to Strata
```

The `afterFileEdit` hook reindexes handoffs, blueprints, plans, and rules on save; bulk or stale indexes need an explicit `strata index`.

## Multi-repo scoped prompts

When the prompt starts with `[repo-a, repo-b]`, run steps 1–2 **per scoped repo**, then step 3 once with the combined task description (graph links across projects).

